---
import ToolPage from '../layouts/ToolPage.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import ToolkitTabs from '../components/ToolkitTabs.astro';

const title = 'Audio Merger - Join Audio Files Online Free | TruePDF';
const description =
  'Join multiple audio clips into one file online for free. Reorder clips, add crossfades at each join, export WAV. No signup, no watermark. Your audio never leaves your browser.';
const h1 = 'Join audio clips';
const lede = 'Stitch voice memos, song parts, or podcast segments into one file, in your order. Free, no account, no watermark.';
---
<ToolPage
  title={title}
  description={description}
  h1={h1}
  lede={lede}
  crumbs={[{ label: 'Media tools', href: '/media-tools' }, { label: 'Audio merger', href: '/audio-merger' }]}
  toolName="TruePDF Audio Merger"
  intro={[
    'Joining audio clips is the kind of job that sounds trivial until a website makes it complicated: upload each file, wait in a queue, sit through an ad, then discover the download has a watermark or a daily limit attached. This merger does the whole thing in your tab. Your files stay on your device, are arranged in your order, joined, and handed back as a download. No queue, no account, nothing uploaded.',
    'The part most mergers get wrong is the join itself. Slamming two clips together usually leaves an audible click where they meet. This tool overlaps the clips slightly and crossfades between them: the outgoing clip fades down as the incoming one fades up, with a blend length you control from zero to five seconds. A half-second blend is enough to kill the click; longer blends sound DJ-style. Prefer a clean dip to quiet between clips instead? Switch the join style to "Fade to quiet".',
    'Clips do not need to match: a phone voice memo and a desktop recording land in the same file without pitch or speed surprises. Pick WAV for a lossless file ready for any editor, or MP3 at 192 kbps when you want a much smaller file for sharing.',
  ]}
  steps={[
    'Drop your audio clips onto the box above, or click it to browse. Add as many as you like, in any order.',
    'Reorder the clips by dragging them, or with the up and down arrows. The number on each row is its position in the final file.',
    'Set the blend length for the joins. Half a second removes clicks; longer blends sound DJ-style. Set it to zero for hard cuts.',
    'Click "Join clips". The merged file is rendered on your device.',
    'Download the result as a WAV or MP3 file, whichever you picked.',
  ]}
  specs={[
    ['Cost', 'Free, no limits'],
    ['Signup', 'None. No account, no email.'],
    ['Watermark', 'None'],
    ['Where files are processed', 'In your browser, on your device'],
    ['Clip limit', 'None enforced. Very long joins are limited only by your device\u2019s memory.'],
    ['Join style', 'Crossfade (clips overlap) or fade-to-quiet, 0 to 5 seconds at each join'],
    ['Mixed formats', 'Different recording types are matched automatically'],
    ['Output', 'WAV (lossless) or MP3'],
    ['Works offline', 'Yes, once the page has loaded'],
  ]}
  faqs={[
    {
      q: 'Is this audio merger really free?',
      a: 'Yes. There is no free tier with a paid tier above it, no daily quota, and no features held back. Joining audio is a small local computation, so there is nothing to charge for. The merged file downloads with no watermark and no account.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Are my audio files uploaded to a server?',
      a: 'No. Your clips are joined entirely in your browser. Nothing is sent anywhere, which makes this safe for voice memos, interviews, and unreleased recordings. Closing the tab removes all trace of the files.',
    },
    {
      q: 'What is the difference between crossfade and fade to quiet?',
      a: 'When two clips meet, the waveform usually jumps from one level to another in a single sample. Your ear hears that jump as a click or pop. Crossfade overlaps the clips slightly and blends from one to the other, so the join disappears completely. "Fade to quiet" instead dips briefly toward silence at each join, which sounds cleaner when the clips are very different, like speech followed by music. Both use the blend length you set.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Can I join clips with different sample rates or formats?',
      a: 'Yes. Clips with different recording settings are matched before joining, so mono and stereo mix fine. The pitch and speed of every clip stay correct.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Should I pick WAV or MP3?',
      a: 'WAV is lossless, so the joined file keeps every sample exactly as rendered, ready for any editor. MP3 at 192 kbps is much smaller and sounds the same to most ears, so pick it when the file is for sharing or listening. Both are made on your device, nothing is uploaded.',
    },
    {
      q: 'How many clips can I join at once?',
      a: 'There is no built-in limit. In practice the limit is your device\u2019s memory, because every clip is read in before joining. Dozens of normal clips join without trouble; hours of audio may slow things down. If a join ever fails, try fewer clips at a time.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Will joining change the sound quality?',
      a: 'Only in the ways you ask for: the fades at the joins. Everything else is joined as-is, so the audio stays at full quality.',
    },
  ]}
>
  <ToolkitTabs
    current="/audio-merger"
    tabs={[
      { href: '/audio-trimmer', label: 'Trim' },
      { href: '/audio-merger', label: 'Merge' },
      { href: '/audio-converter', label: 'Convert' },
    ]}
  />
  <section class="tool-card" slot="tool" aria-label="Audio merger tool">
    <div id="dropzone" class="dropzone" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Add audio clips to join">
      <div class="dz-icon"><Icon name="audio" size={30} /></div>
      <div class="dz-title">Drop audio clips here</div>
      <div class="dz-sub">or click to choose files &middot; they stay on your device</div>
    </div>
    <input type="file" id="file-input" accept="audio/*,.m4a,.ogg,.oga,.flac,.wav,.mp3" multiple hidden />
    <div id="error-box" class="error-box" hidden></div>
    <ul id="file-list" class="file-list"></ul>
    <p id="empty-state" class="empty-state">No clips yet. Add your audio above, then arrange them in order.</p>

    <div class="field field-med">
      <label for="fade-slider">Blend length at each join</label>
      <div class="range-row">
        <input type="range" id="fade-slider" min="0" max="5" step="0.5" value="0.5" />
        <span class="range-val" id="fade-val">0.5s</span>
      </div>
      <p class="hint" id="fade-hint">How long the clips overlap at each join. Half a second blends smoothly; longer overlaps sound DJ-style. Zero means a hard cut.</p>
    </div>

    <h3 class="tool-step">How clips join</h3>
    <div class="radio-cards" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Join style">
      <label class="radio-card"><input type="radio" name="join-style" value="crossfade" checked /><span><strong>Crossfade</strong><small>Clips overlap, blending together.</small></span></label>
      <label class="radio-card"><input type="radio" name="join-style" value="fade" /><span><strong>Fade to quiet</strong><small>Each join dips briefly between clips.</small></span></label>
    </div>

    <h3 class="tool-step">Output format</h3>
    <div class="radio-cards" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Output format">
      <label class="radio-card"><input type="radio" name="out-format" value="wav" checked /><span><strong>WAV</strong><small>Lossless. Big files, best for editing.</small></span></label>
      <label class="radio-card"><input type="radio" name="out-format" value="mp3" /><span><strong>MP3</strong><small>Much smaller. Best for sharing.</small></span></label>
    </div>

    <div class="btn-row">
      <button id="merge-btn" class="btn" disabled>Join clips</button>
      <span id="count-label" class="count-label"></span>
    </div>
    <div id="result" class="result" hidden>
      <h3>Joined</h3>
      <p id="result-info"></p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <script>
    import { initAudioMerger } from '../tools/audio-merger';
    initAudioMerger();
  </script>
</ToolPage>
